This repository adapts work from bdenglish/skills, supplied as a repository
snapshot during development. The Iterate skill and its manifest helper derive
from the original ben-iterate skill. The original human-feedback-first,
six-phase development philosophy is retained.

The earlier adapted Debate method used five reviewers, three reconcilers and one
synthesizer. The current method uses flat independent peers and same-peer ballots;
the earlier hierarchy is historical lineage, not current runtime instructions.
Historical Luna/Terra/Astra selections are reference profiles, not runtime
restrictions. Host mappings do not establish unperformed compatibility checks.
The earlier standalone review application is not part of this distribution.

This repository is independently maintained by mdbecker. Upstream reference:
https://github.com/bdenglish/skills
